      "title_sha256_16": "d8eb32864e2aa5aa",
      "title_text": "Partner interest/remuneration or a mixed interest-and-charges ledger: clause 44 treatment is a CA call, never column 3 or 5",
      "limits_sha256_16": "6a07ddf570a96edf",
      "limits_text": [
        "Interest on a partner's capital and a partner's remuneration are not plainly either an exempt supply (N12 27(a)) or a Schedule III item (a partner is not plainly an 'employee') -- s.7(1)(aa) deems a firm and its partners separate persons, but no circular addresses this specifically. A ledger that books both interest and charges together cannot be divided between column 3 and column 5 from the books alone. Neither is placed in any of the four registration columns here -- the CA must pick one treatment (column 7 or excluded from the base) and disclose it (GN 79.21).",
        "Source: our review of clause 44's money items, Q2 (row: interest on partners' capital) and the final table's own instruction to show a ledger mixing interest and charges separately, both confidence U."
      ],
      "ask_client_sha256_16": "6ece10524040a7a6",
      "ask_client_text": [
        "Confirm and disclose the treatment taken for partner interest/remuneration for clause 44, and identify whether any listed ledger's interest and charges can be shown separately."
      ]
